From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:37:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: let apps that may record windows list, capture and
 overlay them

A game clipper finds the game's window, records only that window and
shows a short hint above it while it is full screen. Mutter offered
neither without the screen cast portal, which asks every time.

ext-foreign-toplevel-list-v1 lists the windows on the taskbar with
their title and the app id the shell attributes them to with
meta_window_set_shell_app_id(), such as steam_app_<id> for a Steam
game whose window calls itself something else, or else their WM_CLASS
or Wayland app id. ext-image-copy-capture-v1 with
ext-foreign-toplevel-image-capture-source-v1 copies a window into a
buffer the client provides, shared memory or a DMA-BUF in ARGB8888 or
XRGB8888, drawing the pointer in when asked, and stops when the window
closes. A DMA-BUF frame is ready once the GPU has finished drawing it,
so clients need no implicit sync, and a frame fails with
buffer_constraints only when its buffer doesn't fit. Window recordings,
the screen cast portal's included, show the window's own picture
without the shell's rounded corners, outline and shadow, and an X11
window's recording is its client area alone, without the frame.
MetaDisplay::window-capture-started and ::window-capture-ended tell
the shell what is recorded, and meta_display_stop_window_capture()
ends a recording. zwlr_layer_shell_v1 offers only the overlay layer:
such a surface sits above every window, fullscreen ones included, and
is never picked, so it takes neither focus nor the pointer.

Sandboxed clients see these globals only while the shell permits their
app window-capture, and starting a recording or an overlay checks it
again.

Upstream-Status: luft-only GNOME offers recording through the screen cast portal instead
